### Quality-attribute scenarios
NFR ids are the PRD's. Scenarios that implement one NFR cite it in Source.

| ID | Attribute | Priority (H/M/L importance / difficulty) | Source | Stimulus | Environment | Artifact | Response | Measure |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| QA-001 | Performance | H/L | prd.md NFR-002, PD-008 | Patient opens the slot picker | 4G phone, 100 concurrent users | ctr-web, cmp-scheduling | Free slots shown | 95% of requests within 2 s |
| QA-002 | Performance | H/L | prd.md NFR-002, PD-008 | Patient confirms a booking | 4G phone, 100 concurrent users | cmp-booking, ctr-db | Booking saved and confirmation screen shown | 95% of requests within 3 s |
| QA-003 | Consistency | H/H | prd.md FR-012, NFR-003, US-012 | Two people confirm the same slot at once | 30 patients booking at once (design 100), plus reception | cmp-booking, ent-appointment | One booking succeeds, the other gets "slot taken" with next free slots | 0 overlapping active appointments for one dentist in 100% of 1,000 concurrent-attempt test runs |
| QA-004 | Reliability | H/H | prd.md NFR-005, PD-001 | A reminder falls due | Normal clinic load, a provider slow or down | cmp-messaging, cmp-channel-adapters | Reminder sent once, in the chosen channel, to a person not opted out, never for a cancelled appointment | 99% sent within 15 minutes of scheduled time per month, 0 sent for cancelled |
| QA-005 | Availability | H/M | prd.md NFR-004, PD-008, A-004 | A patient books at any hour, reception works in clinic hours | Production, one instance or zone lost | ctr-clinic-api, ctr-db | Booking continues | 99.5% a month for online booking; reception screens 08:00–20:00 Monday to Saturday |
| QA-006 | Scalability | M/L | prd.md NFR-003 | Third clinic, 10 dentists, 1,000 appointments a week | Production | ctr-clinic-api, ctr-db | Handled without redesign | 3 clinics, 10 dentists, 1,000 a week and 100 concurrent users meet QA-001 and QA-002 |
| QA-007 | Security | H/M | prd.md NFR-006, FR-004 | A user asks for data outside their role | Production | cmp-identity and every module | Request refused | 0 cross-clinic or cross-patient reads in tests; staff passwords at least 10 characters; all traffic HTTPS; OWASP ASVS L1 |
| QA-008 | Privacy | M/M | prd.md NFR-007 | A patient asks for deletion | Production | cmp-identity, ent-patient | Personal data removed or anonymised | Within 30 days of the request (DPDP Act); only listed fields stored |
| QA-009 | Compliance | M/M | prd.md NFR-011 | A message is sent or a patient replies STOP | Production | cmp-messaging, cmp-channel-adapters | Only registered templates used; opt-out honoured | 100% of SMS via DLT templates, WhatsApp via approved templates; STOP honoured within 1 hour |
| QA-010 | Usability and compatibility | M/L | prd.md NFR-001, NFR-010 | A new patient books | Phone, current Chrome or Safari | ctr-web | Booking completed | 5 screens or fewer after sign-in, tap targets at least 44 px, no sideways scrolling |
| QA-011 | Modifiability | M/L | prd.md FR-001, NFR-003 | The manager adds a third clinic and a dentist | Production | cmp-scheduling | Offered to patients with no code change | 0 deploys, done in the staff screens |
| QA-012 | Localisation | L/L | prd.md NFR-008 | Any screen or message | Production | ctr-web, cmp-messaging | English text, times in IST | 100% of screens and templates English, IST |

Delivery date (NFR-009, release 1 on 1 March 2027) is CON-001; it shapes the style (ADR-0001) and the MVP / R2 split rather than a scenario.

Architectural drivers: QA-003, QA-004.

### Constraints
| ID | Constraint | Kind (technical / regulatory / organizational / budget) |
|---|---|---|
| CON-001 | Release 1 live on 1 March 2027, firm (NFR-009, REQ-019); R2 about 2–3 weeks later | organizational |
| CON-002 | A website only: no native app, no install (NFR-001, REQ-021) | technical |
| CON-003 | SMS only through DLT-registered sender ID and templates; WhatsApp only through approved templates (NFR-011, DEP-001, DEP-002) | regulatory |
| CON-004 | Follow the DPDP Act: store only name, phone, family names and birth years, appointments, treatment type, message choice; delete on request within 30 days (NFR-007) | regulatory |
| CON-005 | English only; all times in IST (NFR-008) | organizational |
| CON-006 | No clinical notes, X-rays, treatment records, prescriptions, payments or insurance (scope out of scope) | organizational |
| CON-007 | SMS and WhatsApp accounts are in the clinic's name; the clinic pays message charges (REQ-029) | budget |
| CON-008 | Hosting in a cloud region in India chosen by us; the clinic provides the domain (SA-002, DEP-004) | technical |

### Assumptions (to confirm with the client)
| ID | Assumption | Affects |
|---|---|---|
| ASM-001 | Q-007 open: one account per phone number with up to 5 family members (SA-001). If families need separate sign-ins on one phone, sign-in and cmp-identity change (RSK-003) | FR-006, FR-025, cmp-identity, ent-patient |
| ASM-002 | Q-008 open: provider chosen at set-up on a managed container service and managed PostgreSQL in an India region; the clinic gives the domain (SA-002) | ctr-web, ctr-clinic-api, ctr-db, ADR-0005 |
| ASM-003 | Q-009 open: quiet hours 21:00–08:00 IST; a reminder due 21:00–24:00 goes at 20:00 the same evening, one due 00:00–08:00 goes at 20:00 the evening before. NFR-005 is measured against this adjusted time. If that time has passed when the booking is made, the reminder goes at once outside quiet hours, otherwise at 08:00 | FR-027, FR-028, QA-004 |
| ASM-004 | Q-015 open: a walk-in is a normal appointment marked arrived (SA-004); it counts in the no-show rate | FR-020, FR-032 |
| ASM-005 | The client has not agreed to the WhatsApp-to-SMS fallback (ISS-001, SA-008); it is built behind a switch, default on, and is R2 | FR-029, FR-033 |
| ASM-006 | NFR-002 and NFR-004 targets are our proposals (PD-008, ISS-004); to confirm at Gate 2 | QA-001, QA-002, QA-005 |
| ASM-007 | Customer-facing defaults: RPO 15 minutes, RTO 1 hour for the database; backups kept 14 days | ctr-db |
| ASM-008 | A patient session lasts 7 days from last use (fewer SMS codes); staff sessions end after 8 hours or 30 minutes idle | FR-002, FR-003 |
| ASM-009 | The chosen SMS and WhatsApp providers offer delivery-receipt webhooks, inbound reply (STOP) forwarding and a test account in week 1–2 (DEP-001, DEP-002) | FR-029, FR-031, rel-009, rel-010 |
| ASM-010 | "Within the next 30 days" means today and the 30 days after (1 March shows up to 31 March, US-011.AC3); the horizon is a setting | FR-011 |
| ASM-011 | Receptionists may search all patients by phone or name (a patient is not tied to one clinic), but see appointments of their own clinic only | FR-020, FR-004, NFR-006 |
| ASM-012 | Appointments and history are kept 24 months, then personal data is anonymised; messages are kept 90 days; the 12-month report and the 6-month block need no more | NFR-007, ent-appointment, ent-message |
| ASM-013 | Deletion on request is done by the practice manager in an admin screen (not in the PRD's FRs, added for NFR-007) | QA-008, cmp-identity |
| ASM-014 | A reception cancel records "cancelled by the patient" when the patient asked, otherwise "cancelled by the clinic"; the no-show rate excludes both | FR-020, FR-024, FR-032 |
| ASM-015 | No-show baseline (PRD Questions to raise, item 1): the first 2 months of app data; the system provides the rate from go-live | FR-032 |

## 3. Solution strategy

A **modular monolith** (ADR-0001): one API deployable with eight capability modules and one PostgreSQL database, plus a static single-page web app. It beats the next-simpler style (a layered monolith without module boundaries) because R2 modules (MOD-06, MOD-08) ship after the MVP and a third clinic must arrive as data (QA-011); it beats microservices because the two drivers need one transaction, not a saga (QA-003), and the team is small with a firm date (CON-001).

| Pattern | Driver that needs it | Where |
|---|---|---|
| Layers (entry, business, data) in the one deployable | Always | ctr-clinic-api |
| Database exclusion constraint on overlapping appointments (ADR-0003) | QA-003 | ent-appointment in ctr-db |
| Message rows with a precomputed send time, claimed by a dispatcher (ADR-0002, ADR-0009) | QA-004 | cmp-messaging, ent-message |
| Ports and adapters (ADR-0006), one adapter per external provider | QA-009, QA-004: two providers, one core | cmp-channel-adapters |
| Retry with backoff, timeout, circuit breaker on provider calls | QA-004, QA-005 | cmp-channel-adapters |
| Idempotent webhooks and idempotent sends | QA-004 | cmp-messaging, cmp-channel-adapters |
| Role-based access with clinic scoping in each module | QA-007 | cmp-identity and every module |
| Account and person split (ADR-0008) | FR-006, FR-025, PD-007 | ent-patient-account, ent-patient |
| Static CDN delivery, cookie session (ADR-0004) | QA-001, QA-010, QA-007 | ctr-web |

Not used, and why: no message broker (volume about 1,000 reminders a week, ADR-0002), no cache (live queries meet QA-001 at this size), no API gateway (one deployable), no CQRS or event sourcing (the history table in FR-024 is an audit log, not the source of state), no Kubernetes (ADR-0005).

