  9913:           "req_id": "NFR-007",
  9940:           "text": "Given a patient account exists for a phone number, When the patient enters the number and asks for a code, Then a 6-digit code is sent by SMS and the screen asks for the code. (source: FR-002)"
  9945:           "text": "Given a code was sent less than 10 minutes ago, When the patient enters it correctly, Then the patient is signed in and sees their own appointments area. (source: FR-002)"
  9950:           "text": "Given a code was sent, When the patient enters a wrong code, Then the screen says the code is wrong, shows how to get a new code, and the wrong try is counted. (source: FR-002)"
  9955:           "text": "Given a code was sent more than 10 minutes ago, When the patient enters it, Then the screen says the code has expired and offers a new code. (source: FR-002)"
  9960:           "text": "Given a patient has entered 5 wrong codes for a phone number, When they try again within 15 minutes (with the old or a new code), Then the system refuses and says to wait, and after 15 minutes a new code can be requested. (source: FR-002, NFR-006)"
  9965:           "text": "Given a patient has not used the site for less than 7 days, When they return, Then they are still signed in; **Given** 7 days without use, **Then** they must sign in again. (source: FR-002)"
  9970:           "text": "Given a single network address or a single day has produced too many code requests, When another code is requested, Then the request is refused without sending an SMS. (source: NFR-006)"
  10013:           "req_id": "FR-002",
  10018:           "req_id": "NFR-006",
  10045:           "text": "Given a phone number with no account, When the patient verifies a correct code, Then the screen asks for their name and no account exists yet. (source: FR-002)"
  10050:           "text": "Given the code is verified for a new number, When the patient gives a name, Then one account for that phone number and one person record with that name are created and the patient is signed in. (source: FR-002, NFR-007)"
  10055:           "text": "Given the code for a new number is wrong or expired, When the patient continues, Then no account is created. (source: FR-002)"
  10060:           "text": "Given the name is empty, When the patient submits, Then the screen asks for a name and creates nothing. (source: FR-002)"
  10065:           "text": "Given an account already exists for the phone number, When a patient signs in with it, Then no second account is created. (source: FR-002)"
  10102:           "req_id": "FR-002",
  10107:           "req_id": "NFR-007",
  10134:           "text": "Given an active staff account, When the person enters the correct username and password, Then they are signed in and land on the screen for their role. (source: FR-003)"
  10139:           "text": "Given an active staff account, When a wrong password is entered, Then the screen says the username or password is wrong without saying which one. (source: FR-003, NFR-006)"
  10144:           "text": "Given 5 failed sign-ins for a username, When a sixth is tried within 15 minutes (even with the right password), Then it is refused with a message to wait; after 15 minutes sign-in works again. (source: NFR-006)"
  10149:           "text": "Given a staff member is signed in, When 30 minutes pass without use or 8 hours pass since sign-in, Then the next request requires signing in again. (source: FR-003)"
  10154:           "text": "Given a password is set or changed, When it has fewer than 10 characters, Then it is rejected. (source: NFR-006)"
  10159:           "text": "Given any screen or call, When it is reached over plain HTTP, Then it is not served; all traffic is over HTTPS. (source: NFR-006)"
  10164:           "text": "Given a signed-in staff member, When they change their own password (giving the current one) or the manager sets a new password for them, Then the new password works at the next sign-in and the old one does not. (source: FR-003, FR-005)"
  10201:           "req_id": "FR-003",
  10206:           "req_id": "NFR-006",
  10211:           "req_id": "FR-005",
  10240:           "text": "Given a patient is signed in, When they ask for an appointment of a person who is not themselves or one of their family members, Then the system refuses it as if it did not exist. (source: FR-004, NFR-006)"
  10245:           "text": "Given a receptionist of clinic A, When they ask for or change an appointment of clinic B, Then the system refuses. (source: FR-004, NFR-006)"
  10250:           "text": "Given a receptionist of clinic A, When they search patients by phone number or name, Then they find patients regardless of clinic but see appointments of clinic A only. (source: FR-004)"
  10255:           "text": "Given a dentist is signed in, When they ask for another dentist's day or try to change anything, Then the system refuses. (source: FR-004)"
  10260:           "text": "Given the practice manager is signed in, When they open data of either clinic or the settings, Then it is allowed. (source: FR-004)"
  10265:           "text": "Given a person's role, clinic or active flag changed since they signed in, When they make their next request, Then the current values apply at once. (source: FR-004, FR-005)"
  10270:           "text": "Given a request without sign-in, or one that changes data without coming from the BrightSmile website, When it is made, Then it is refused. (source: NFR-006)"
  10315:           "req_id": "FR-004",
  10320:           "req_id": "NFR-006",
  10325:           "req_id": "FR-005",
  10352:           "text": "Given the manager is on the staff screen, When they create a receptionist with name, username, initial password and clinic, Then the account exists, is active and is assigned to that clinic. (source: FR-005)"
  10357:           "text": "Given the manager creates a dentist account, When it is saved, Then the dentist can sign in and see their own day. (source: FR-005)"
  10362:           "text": "Given a receptionist is assigned to one clinic, When the manager assigns them to another clinic, Then the receptionist's access follows the new clinic at once. (source: FR-005, FR-004)"
  10367:           "text": "Given an active staff account, When the manager deactivates it, Then the person cannot sign in and an existing session is refused on its next request. (source: FR-005)"
  10372:           "text": "Given a username already exists, When the manager creates another with the same username, Then the system refuses. (source: FR-005)"
  10377:           "text": "Given a person who is not the practice manager, When they try to create, change or deactivate a staff account, Then the system refuses. (source: FR-005, FR-004)"
  10382:           "text": "Given the manager is the only active manager, When they try to deactivate their own account, Then the system refuses. (source: FR-005)"
  10419:           "req_id": "FR-005",
  10424:           "req_id": "FR-004",
  10429:           "req_id": "NFR-006",
  10456:           "text": "Given the manager is on the erasure screen, When they find a patient account by phone number and confirm erasure, Then the request is recorded with its date and the account can no longer sign in. (source: NFR-007)"
  10461:           "text": "Given an erasure was confirmed, When the process completes (within 30 days of the request), Then the account, the person records of the account holder and family members, and the stored messages hold no name, phone number or birth year. (source: NFR-007)"
  10466:           "text": "Given the erased patient had appointments, When erasure completes, Then the appointment rows remain without any personal link. (source: NFR-007)"
  10471:           "text": "Given the system stores personal data, When the stored fields are reviewed, Then only name, phone number, family members' names and birth years, appointments, treatment type and message choice are held; no clinical data. (source: NFR-007)"
  10476:           "text": "Given a signed-in user who is not the practice manager, When they try to use erasure, Then it is refused. (source: NFR-007, FR-004)"
  10481:           "text": "Given logs are inspected, When any sign-in or erasure activity is searched, Then no name, phone number or birth year appears. (source: NFR-007)"
  10486:           "text": "Given sign-in codes and old personal data exist, When retention periods pass (sign-in codes 24 hours, accounts idle for 24 months, staff 24 months after deactivation), Then they are deleted or anonymised; messages (90 days) and appointments (24 months) follow the same rule in the features that own them. (source: NFR-007)"
  10523:           "req_id": "NFR-007",
  10528:           "req_id": "FR-004",
  10534:         "Priority raised from should/P2 to must/P1: NFR-007 is a DPDP Act requirement and the spec says it must be ready by go-live on 1 March 2027 (not listed in DL-1 requirement ids). Confirm with the PM."
  10557:           "text": "Given a receptionist finds a patient account by phone number or name, When they deactivate it, Then the patient cannot sign in and an open session is refused on its next request. (source: NFR-006)"
  10562:           "text": "Given a deactivated patient account, When the practice manager reactivates it, Then the patient can sign in again. (source: NFR-006)"
  10567:           "text": "Given a dentist or a patient, When they try to deactivate a patient account, Then it is refused. (source: NFR-006, FR-004)"
