  16288:           "req_id": "FR-008",
  16293:           "req_id": "FR-009",
  16298:           "req_id": "FR-010",
  16325:           "text": "Given the practice manager is signed in and 2 active clinics exist, When they add a clinic with a name, address and phone number, Then the clinic is saved as active and appears in the clinic list for all roles without any deploy. (source: FR-001)"
  16330:           "text": "Given a dentist exists, When the manager edits the dentist's name or marks the dentist inactive, Then the change is saved and an inactive dentist is no longer offered for new bookings. (source: FR-001)"
  16335:           "text": "Given a clinic or dentist that has appointments, When the manager marks it inactive, Then existing appointments are kept unchanged and the record is not deleted. (source: FR-001)"
  16340:           "text": "Given a signed-in receptionist, dentist or patient, When they try to add, edit or deactivate a clinic or a dentist, Then the system refuses and nothing changes. (source: FR-001)"
  16345:           "text": "Given a clinic name already in use by an active clinic, When the manager saves a second clinic with the same name, Then the system refuses it and says why. (source: FR-001)"
  16382:           "req_id": "FR-001",
  16409:           "text": "Given the system is set up, When any signed-in user asks for the treatment list, Then check-up, cleaning and consultation are present as online types of 30 minutes each. (source: FR-009)"
  16414:           "text": "Given the manager is signed in, When they add a treatment type with a name, a duration and the online flag off, Then the type is saved and is visible to reception but not to patients. (source: FR-009)"
  16419:           "text": "Given a treatment type, When the manager changes its duration or online flag, Then the change applies to slots and bookings made from then on and does not change existing appointments. (source: FR-009)"
  16424:           "text": "Given a treatment type, When the manager marks it inactive, Then it is no longer offered for new bookings and existing appointments keep it. (source: FR-009)"
  16429:           "text": "Given a duration that is not a positive multiple of 30 minutes, When the manager saves a treatment type, Then the system refuses it and says why. (source: FR-009, FR-010)"
  16434:           "text": "Given a signed-in receptionist, dentist or patient, When they try to add or edit a treatment type, Then the system refuses it. (source: FR-009)"
  16471:           "req_id": "FR-009",
  16476:           "req_id": "FR-010",
  16503:           "text": "Given a dentist and a clinic, When the manager sets Monday 09:00–17:00 with a break 13:00–14:00, Then the hours and the break are saved and shown again when the week is opened. (source: FR-007)"
  16508:           "text": "Given a dentist who works Monday at clinic A, When the manager adds Thursday hours at clinic B, Then both are kept and the dentist is shown as working at both clinics on those days. (source: FR-001, FR-007)"
  16513:           "text": "Given a dentist with hours at clinic A on Monday 09:00–17:00, When the manager saves Monday 15:00–19:00 for the same dentist at clinic B, Then the system refuses it because the dentist cannot be at two clinics at the same time. (source: FR-001, FR-007)"
  16518:           "text": "Given a weekday's hours, When the manager enters an end that is not after the start, a break outside the hours, or two overlapping breaks, Then the system refuses it and names the problem. (source: FR-007)"
  16523:           "text": "Given a dentist with weekly hours, When the manager removes a weekday's hours (a day off), Then that weekday no longer produces free slots for that dentist at that clinic. (source: FR-007)"
  16528:           "text": "Given a signed-in receptionist, dentist or patient, When they try to change weekly hours, Then the system refuses it. A receptionist or dentist may read hours. (source: FR-007)"
  16533:           "text": "Given appointments already booked outside newly changed hours, When the manager saves the change, Then the hours are saved and the system does not move or cancel those appointments. (source: FR-007, FR-008)"
  16570:           "req_id": "FR-007",
  16575:           "req_id": "FR-001",
  16580:           "req_id": "FR-008",
  16607:           "text": "Given a dentist working Monday 09:00–17:00 at a clinic with a break 13:00–14:00, When free 30-minute slots are requested for that Monday, Then slots start at 09:00, 09:30 and so on on the hour or half hour, none start in 13:00–13:59, and the last one starts at 16:30. (source: FR-010)"
  16612:           "text": "Given the same dentist with an appointment booked 10:00–10:30, When slots are requested, Then the 10:00 slot is not offered and 10:30 is. (source: FR-010)"
  16617:           "text": "Given the same dentist is booked at another clinic on that Monday at 11:00–11:30, When slots are requested for this clinic, Then the 11:00 slot is not offered. (source: FR-010, FR-001)"
  16622:           "text": "Given leave recorded for that dentist from 15:00 to 16:00 on that Monday, When slots are requested, Then no slot overlaps 15:00–16:00. (source: FR-010, FR-008)"
  16627:           "text": "Given a 90-minute treatment, When slots are requested, Then a slot is offered only if the whole 90 minutes fit in working time without touching a break, leave or booked appointment. (source: FR-010, FR-009)"
  16632:           "text": "Given a signed-in patient, When they ask for slots, Then only online treatment types are accepted, only slots from now up to the end of the booking horizon are returned, and only active clinics and dentists are included. (source: FR-010, FR-009)"
  16637:           "text": "Given a clinic with several dentists, When \"first available\" is requested, Then the 10 earliest free slots across the clinic's dentists are returned in time order, each with its dentist, and asking for the next page returns the following 10. (source: FR-010)"
  16642:           "text": "Given a date range with no free slot, When slots are requested, Then an empty list is returned (not an error). (source: FR-010)"
  16647:           "text": "Given a request for slots at a clinic or dentist that is inactive, or a treatment type that is inactive, When it is made, Then no slots are returned. (source: FR-010, FR-001)"
  16652:           "text": "Given a booking made by another part of the system just before the request, When slots are requested, Then that appointment is already excluded. (source: FR-010)"
  16689:           "req_id": "FR-010",
  16694:           "req_id": "FR-001",
  16699:           "req_id": "FR-008",
  16704:           "req_id": "FR-009",
  16731:           "text": "Given a dentist, When the manager records leave for whole days from a first day to a last day, Then the leave is saved from the start of the first day to the end of the last day in India time. (source: FR-008)"
  16736:           "text": "Given a dentist, When the manager records part-day leave with a date, a start time and an end time, Then the leave is saved for exactly that time. (source: FR-008)"
  16741:           "text": "Given booked appointments that overlap the new leave, When the leave is saved, Then the response and screen list each of those appointments (date, time, clinic, patient name, phone number, treatment) and the system does not change any of them. (source: FR-008)"
  16746:           "text": "Given an appointment that only partly overlaps the leave, When the leave is saved, Then that appointment is listed too. (source: FR-008)"
  16751:           "text": "Given cancelled appointments or appointments outside the leave time, When the leave is saved, Then they are not listed. (source: FR-008)"
  16756:           "text": "Given saved leave, When free slots are requested for those days, Then no slot overlaps the leave. (source: FR-008, FR-010)"
  16761:           "text": "Given a leave end that is not after its start, or a leave that has already ended, When the manager saves it, Then the system refuses it and says why. (source: FR-008)"
  16766:           "text": "Given leave entered by mistake, When the manager deletes it, Then slots in that time come back and the appointments are no longer on any to-move list because of it. (source: FR-008)"
  16771:           "text": "Given a signed-in receptionist, dentist or patient, When they try to record or delete leave, Then the system refuses it. (source: FR-008)"
  16798:         "rationale": "No history; ~34h over 12 tasks: IST-to-UTC leave intervals, read-only overlap selection via port, 24-month retention job, leave page. FR-008 is in Release 1 (DL-1), so must despite spec P2."
  16808:           "req_id": "FR-008",
  16813:           "req_id": "FR-010",
  16840:           "text": "Given leave that covers booked appointments at the receptionist's clinic, When the receptionist opens the to-move list, Then those appointments are listed with date, time, dentist, patient name, phone number and treatment, earliest first. (source: FR-008)"
  16845:           "text": "Given leave that also covers appointments at another clinic, When the receptionist asks for the list, Then only their own clinic's appointments are returned, and asking for another clinic is refused. (source: FR-008)"
  16850:           "text": "Given an appointment on the list, When it is moved to a time outside the leave or cancelled, Then it no longer appears on the next read. (source: FR-008)"
  16855:           "text": "Given nothing to move, When the list is opened, Then it says there is nothing to move. (source: FR-008)"
  16860:           "text": "Given the practice manager is signed in, When they ask for the to-move list of any clinic, Then it is returned. (source: FR-008)"
  16865:           "text": "Given a patient or dentist role, When they ask for the to-move list, Then the system refuses it. (source: FR-008)"
  16892:         "rationale": "No history; ~18h over 7 tasks reusing US5 selection logic and ToMoveTable; adds own-clinic scoping and role-based route table. FR-008 is Release 1."
