  43: | FR-001 | The system holds the clinics (2 now; a third is added as data) and the dentists. A dentist can work at more than one clinic, on set days. Every appointment belongs to one clinic and one dentist. | REQ-018 | MOD-01 |
  44: | FR-002 | A patient signs in with their phone number and a one-time code sent by SMS (SA-006). The code is valid for 10 minutes and allows 5 wrong tries, after which the patient waits 15 minutes (PD-006). A new phone number creates an account after the code is verified and the patient gives their name. | REQ-023 | MOD-01 |
  45: | FR-003 | Receptionists, dentists and the practice manager sign in with a username and password. | REQ-026 | MOD-01 |
  46: | FR-004 | Each role sees only what it needs. A patient sees only their own appointments and those of their family members. A receptionist sees and changes the appointments of their own clinic only. A dentist sees their own day, read only. The practice manager sees both clinics and the settings. | REQ-026, REQ-027 | MOD-01 |
  47: | FR-005 | The practice manager creates and deactivates the accounts of receptionists and dentists and assigns receptionists to a clinic. A deactivated person cannot sign in. | REQ-026 | MOD-01 |
  48: | FR-006 | A patient can add up to 5 family members to their account (name and birth year) and book for any of them (SA-001; Q-007 is open). Each booking names the person it is for. | REQ-003, REQ-023 | MOD-01 |
  49: | FR-007 | The practice manager sets each dentist's weekly working hours at each clinic, with breaks. | REQ-013 | MOD-02 |
  50: | FR-008 | The practice manager records a dentist's leave (whole days or part days). Appointments already booked in that time are listed for reception to move; the system never moves them by itself. | REQ-013 | MOD-02 |
  51: | FR-009 | The system holds the treatment types with their duration and whether patients can book them online. Online types are check-up, cleaning and consultation, 30 minutes each. Other types (for example root canal, extraction) are 60 or 90 minutes and are booked by reception only. The practice manager can edit the list. | REQ-014 | MOD-02 |
  52: | FR-010 | Free slots are the dentist's working hours at that clinic minus breaks, leave and booked appointments. Slots start on the hour or half hour. | REQ-013, REQ-014 | MOD-02 |
  53: | FR-011 | A signed-in patient books online: clinic, an online treatment type, a dentist or "first available", then a free slot within the next 30 days (SA-007, PD-002). "First available" shows the earliest free slots across that clinic's dentists. | REQ-003 | MOD-03 |
  54: | FR-012 | A slot is never booked twice. If another booking takes the slot while the patient is choosing, the patient is told and shown the next free slots. | REQ-003 | MOD-03 |
  55: | FR-013 | When booking, the patient chooses SMS or WhatsApp for messages about this appointment. The choice is remembered for their next booking. The first default is SMS. | REQ-012 | MOD-07 |
  56: | FR-014 | On booking, the patient gets a confirmation at once in the chosen channel: clinic, dentist, treatment, date, time and a link to the appointment. | REQ-016 | MOD-07 |
  57: | FR-015 | A signed-in patient sees their upcoming and past appointments (and their family members'), with status. | REQ-004, REQ-005 | MOD-04 |
  58: | FR-016 | A patient can reschedule an upcoming appointment to another free slot (same clinic and treatment; any dentist) until 4 hours before its start. | REQ-004, REQ-006 | MOD-04 |
  59: | FR-017 | A patient can cancel an upcoming appointment until 4 hours before its start. Inside 4 hours the page shows the clinic's phone number instead of the buttons. | REQ-005, REQ-006 | MOD-04 |
  60: | FR-018 | After a cancel or reschedule the freed slot is bookable at once, and the patient gets a message in their chosen channel. | REQ-004, REQ-005, REQ-016 | MOD-04 |
  61: | FR-019 | A receptionist sees the day view of their clinic: one column per dentist working that day, each appointment with patient name, phone number, treatment and status. They can move to other days. | REQ-007 | MOD-05 |
  62: | FR-020 | A receptionist books, reschedules and cancels appointments for patients of their clinic, including reception-only treatment types and walk-ins (SA-004), with no 4-hour cut-off. They find a patient by phone number or name, or create one with name and phone number. | REQ-010, REQ-014, REQ-030 | MOD-05 |
  63: | FR-021 | A receptionist marks a patient as arrived. | REQ-009 | MOD-05 |
  64: | FR-022 | A receptionist marks a patient as a no-show from 15 minutes after the start time until the end of that day, and can undo it the same day (PD-003). | REQ-008 | MOD-05 |
  65: | FR-023 | A dentist sees their own day at each clinic they work at that day, read only: time, patient name, treatment, status. | REQ-027 | MOD-05 |
  66: | FR-024 | An appointment's status is booked, arrived, no-show, cancelled by the patient or cancelled by the clinic. Every change records who made it and when. | REQ-007, REQ-008, REQ-009 | MOD-05 |
  67: | FR-025 | A patient with 2 no-shows in the last 6 months cannot book or reschedule online; the page says to phone the clinic. Their existing bookings stay. Family members' no-shows count against the person who had them (PD-007). | REQ-015 | MOD-06 |
  68: | FR-026 | Reception sees that a patient is blocked, and can lift the block; lifting starts the count again from zero. | REQ-015 | MOD-06 |
  69: | FR-027 | The patient gets a reminder 24 hours before the appointment in the chosen channel. A reminder due between 21:00 and 08:00 India time is sent at 20:00 the evening before (SA-003; Q-009 is open). | REQ-011, REQ-012 | MOD-07 |
  70: | FR-028 | A reminder is not sent for a cancelled appointment. A rescheduled appointment gets a reminder for its new time only. An appointment booked less than 24 hours ahead gets no reminder, only the confirmation. | REQ-011 | MOD-07 |
  71: | FR-029 | If a WhatsApp message cannot be delivered, it is sent once by SMS instead (SA-008, PD-005). If the SMS also fails, the appointment is marked "reminder failed". | REQ-011, REQ-012 | MOD-07 |
  72: | FR-030 | Every reminder says the clinic, dentist, date and time, and has a link to reschedule or cancel. | REQ-011 | MOD-07 |
  73: | FR-031 | A patient can stop reminders by replying STOP, or by asking reception, who switches them off in the patient's record. Confirmations of a booking or a change are still sent. | REQ-011, REQ-012 | MOD-07 |
  74: | FR-032 | The practice manager sees, for each clinic and each of the last 12 months, the number of no-shows and the no-show rate (no-shows ÷ appointments that were not cancelled). On screen only. | REQ-028 | MOD-08 |
  75: | FR-033 | Reception sees the list of tomorrow's appointments whose reminder failed, so they can phone those patients. | REQ-011 | MOD-07 |
