  464: Depends on: S-002-US4 · Sources: NFR-007, FR-004
  466: - [AC-S-002-US6-1] Given the manager is on the erasure screen, When they find a patient account by phone number and confirm erasure, Then the request is recorded with its date and the account can no longer sign in. (source: NFR-007)
  467: - [AC-S-002-US6-2] Given an erasure was confirmed, When the process completes (within 30 days of the request), Then the account, the person records of the account holder and family members, and the stored messages hold no name, phone number or birth year. (source: NFR-007)
  468: - [AC-S-002-US6-3] Given the erased patient had appointments, When erasure completes, Then the appointment rows remain without any personal link. (source: NFR-007)
  469: - [AC-S-002-US6-4] Given the system stores personal data, When the stored fields are reviewed, Then only name, phone number, family members' names and birth years, appointments, treatment type and message choice are held; no clinical data. (source: NFR-007)
  470: - [AC-S-002-US6-5] Given a signed-in user who is not the practice manager, When they try to use erasure, Then it is refused. (source: NFR-007, FR-004)
  471: - [AC-S-002-US6-6] Given logs are inspected, When any sign-in or erasure activity is searched, Then no name, phone number or birth year appears. (source: NFR-007)
  472: - [AC-S-002-US6-7] Given sign-in codes and old personal data exist, When retention periods pass (sign-in codes 24 hours, accounts idle for 24 months, staff 24 months after deactivation), Then they are deleted or anonymised; messages (90 days) and appointments (24 months) follow the same rule in the features that own them. (source: NFR-007)
