  490: - [AC-S-002-US7-1] Given a receptionist finds a patient account by phone number or name, When they deactivate it, Then the patient cannot sign in and an open session is refused on its next request. (source: NFR-006)
  491: - [AC-S-002-US7-2] Given a deactivated patient account, When the practice manager reactivates it, Then the patient can sign in again. (source: NFR-006)
  492: - [AC-S-002-US7-3] Given a dentist or a patient, When they try to deactivate a patient account, Then it is refused. (source: NFR-006, FR-004)
