  881: | 004-T062 | Run the load script and the 4G check on staging and record results against NFR-0 | 7.0 | qa-automation, docs | no | 004-T058, 004-T059, 004-T061 |
  885: Depends on: - · Sources: E-004, FR-011, FR-012, FR-013, NFR-002
  897: Depends on: S-SETUP-004, S-FOUND-001 · Sources: E-004, FR-011, FR-012, FR-013, NFR-002
  919: Depends on: S-004-US1, S-004-US2, S-004-US3, S-004-US4, S-004-US5 · Sources: E-004, FR-011, FR-012, NFR-010
  1350: Depends on: S-007-US2 · Sources: FR-028, NFR-005
  1353: - [AC-S-007-US3-2] Given a reminder that is due now but not yet sent, When the appointment is cancelled one second before the send attempt, Then the send is skipped because the appointment is checked again immediately before sending. (source: FR-028, NFR-005)
  1369: Depends on: S-007-US2 · Sources: FR-031, NFR-011
  1374: - [AC-S-007-US4-4] Given a STOP reply, When it is received, Then it takes effect within 1 hour at the latest (the design target is at once). (source: NFR-011)
  1375: - [AC-S-007-US4-5] Given a STOP notification that is not properly signed or comes from a number with no account, When it arrives, Then it is rejected or ignored and no setting changes. (source: FR-031, NFR-011)
  1391: Depends on: S-007-US3 · Sources: NFR-005, NFR-011
  1393: - [AC-S-007-US5-1] Given normal load, When reminders fall due, Then at least 99% in a month are sent within 15 minutes of their adjusted due time. (source: NFR-005)
  1394: - [AC-S-007-US5-2] Given the provider times out or errors, When a message is sent, Then it is retried (3 attempts, waiting 5 s then 30 s between them) and stays queued if the provider is still unavailable, rather than being dropped. (source: NFR-005)
  1395: - [AC-S-007-US5-3] Given many consecutive provider failures (5 within 1 minute), When further messages are due, Then sending to that provider pauses briefly and messages stay queued, and sending resumes when the provider recovers. (source: NFR-005)
  1396: - [AC-S-007-US5-4] Given the same message is processed twice (restart, two API instances, repeated provider notification), When it is sent, Then the patient receives it only once, and a repeated delivery receipt changes nothing. (source: NFR-005)
  1397: - [AC-S-007-US5-5] Given the oldest due, unsent message is more than 10 minutes late, When the lag is measured, Then an alert is raised. (source: NFR-005)
  1398: - [AC-S-007-US5-6] Given the nightly check, When it finds an appointment that should have a reminder but has none, or a message stuck in progress, Then it repairs it and reports the count. (source: NFR-005)
  1399: - [AC-S-007-US5-7] Given any message to be sent, When its kind and channel have no approved template configured, Then it is not sent and the problem is reported; SMS goes only through the registered sender ID and DLT templates, and WhatsApp only through approved templates. (source: NFR-011)
  1400: - [AC-S-007-US5-8] Given a provider call, When it is made, Then only the templated values (clinic, dentist, date, time, link) and the phone number are sent, and no patient name, phone number or message text appears in logs. (source: NFR-011)
  1401: - [AC-S-007-US5-9] Given a delivery receipt that is unsigned or refers to an unknown message, When it arrives, Then it is rejected or ignored. (source: NFR-011)
  1402: - [AC-S-007-US5-10] Given messages older than 90 days, When the retention job runs, Then they are deleted. (source: NFR-011)
  1419: Depends on: S-FOUND-007 · Sources: NFR-011
  1421: - [AC-S-007-US6-1] Given the message kinds and channels, When the template catalogue is reviewed, Then there is one English template for each kind and channel in use, each using only the allowed fields, ready for submission. (source: NFR-011)
  1422: - [AC-S-007-US6-2] Given the catalogue, When the clinic (with our help) submits DLT registration and the WhatsApp templates, Then each submission, date, owner and status is tracked. (source: NFR-011)
  1423: - [AC-S-007-US6-3] Given staging, When a booking is made, Then messages go to provider sandbox accounts and never to real patients. (source: NFR-011)
  1424: - [AC-S-007-US6-4] Given the production configuration, When the readiness check runs, Then it lists any template that is not approved or has no identifier configured, and the go-live decision uses that list. (source: NFR-011)
  1425: - [AC-S-007-US6-5] Given the chosen providers are not yet decided, When the work starts, Then the provider-specific parts are isolated in one adapter per provider so a provider can be replaced without changing the rest. (source: NFR-011; see Assumptions)
  1440: Depends on: S-FOUND-007 · Sources: NFR-011, FR-031
  1442: - [AC-S-007-US7-1] Given the sign-in feature requests a code for a phone number, When the request is made, Then the SMS is sent during that request and the caller learns at once whether the provider accepted it. (source: NFR-011)
  1443: - [AC-S-007-US7-2] Given the SMS provider is down or times out, When a code is requested, Then the caller gets a clear "could not send" result within the timeout and the code is not queued for later delivery. (source: NFR-011)
  1444: - [AC-S-007-US7-3] Given a sign-in code message, When it is recorded, Then the code itself is not kept in readable form in the message record or any log. (source: NFR-011)
  1496: Depends on: - · Sources: E-007, NFR-005, NFR-011
  1509: Depends on: S-SETUP-007 · Sources: E-007, NFR-005, NFR-011
  1543: Depends on: S-007-US4, S-007-US6, S-007-US9 · Sources: E-007, NFR-005, NFR-011
  1563: Depends on: S-FOUND-008, S-002-US2 · Sources: FR-006, NFR-007
  1568: - [AC-S-008-US1-4] Given a signed-in patient, When they add a family member, Then only a name and a birth year are stored for that person (no phone number, no other personal details). (source: FR-006, NFR-007)
  1590: Depends on: S-FOUND-008, S-004-US1 · Sources: FR-006, FR-004, NFR-006
  1613: Depends on: S-FOUND-008, S-005-US1 · Sources: FR-006, FR-004, FR-015, NFR-006
  1617: - [AC-S-008-US3-3] Given two different accounts, When one patient opens their list or asks for an appointment of the other account, Then the other account's appointments are never shown and the request is refused. (source: FR-004, NFR-006)
  1657: Depends on: S-SETUP-008 · Sources: E-008, FR-006, FR-004, NFR-006
  1672: Depends on: S-008-US1, S-008-US2, S-008-US3, S-008-US4 · Sources: E-008, FR-006, NFR-007, NFR-006
