/outputs/clinic-test-2/prd.md:
  19: | Reduce no-shows (same goal) | REQ-002 | Share of due reminders sent within 15 minutes of their due time | At least 99% (PD-001, NFR-005) |
  127: | NFR-001 | compatibility | A mobile-friendly website; no install and no native app. Reception and the practice manager use a desktop browser. | Every patient screen works on a phone without sideways scrolling in current Chrome and Safari on Android and iPhone (A-001) | REQ-017, REQ-021 |
  128: | NFR-002 | performance | Slot lists and the day view load quickly on a phone network. | Free slots shown within 2 s and a booking confirmed within 3 s, for 95% of requests on 4G (PD-008) | REQ-017 |
  129: | NFR-003 | scalability | Handles today's load and a third clinic without redesign. | 2 clinics, 6 dentists, ~450 appointments a week now; 3 clinics, 10 dentists, 1,000 appointments a week later; 30 patients booking at the same time | REQ-018 |
  130: | NFR-004 | availability | Online booking is available at any time; reception screens during clinic hours. | 99.5% per month for online booking; reception screens 08:00–20:00 Monday to Saturday (A-004, PD-008) | REQ-001 |
  131: | NFR-005 | reliability | Reminders go out on time. | 99% of due reminders sent within 15 minutes of their due time; none sent for cancelled appointments (PD-001) | REQ-011 |
  132: | NFR-006 | security | Role separation and safe sign-in. | Receptionists can reach only their own clinic's data; code limits as FR-002; staff passwords at least 10 characters; all traffic over HTTPS | REQ-023, REQ-026 |
  133: | NFR-007 | privacy | Store only what is needed; follow the DPDP Act. | Only name, phone number, family members' names and birth years, appointments, treatment type and message choice are stored; no clinical data; a patient's data is deleted on request within 30 days (A-003) | REQ-025 |
  134: | NFR-008 | localisation | English only; India time. | All screens and messages in English; times in IST | REQ-024 |
