2026-11-16 14:03:25,034 INFO deepagent.transcript: [tool] /outputs/clinic-test-2/architecture.md:
  388: CI/CD: per commit, build → unit tests → contract tests against `contracts/clinic-api-v1.openapi.yaml` → image scan → deploy to staging → smoke test (health, sign-in with test code, book and cancel against sandbox providers) → deploy to prod by rolling replacement, one replica at a time behind the health check. Database changes are forward-only migrations that stay compatible with the previous release (expand, then contract). The web app is built and published separately, with the previous build kept. Rollback trigger: `GET /health` fails, 5xx rate above 2% for 5 minutes, or reminder lag above 15 minutes after a deploy; rollback is redeploying the previous image and the previous static build. Releases: MVP for 1 March 2027, R2 about 2–3 weeks later; R2 screens are hidden by a feature flag until their data is ready.
/outputs/clinic-test-2/backlog/backlog.json:
  8142:       "title": "Create the feature flag models in clinic-api/src/clinic_api/db/models/feature_flag.py",
  8143:       "description_md": "Create the feature flag models in clinic-api/src/clinic_api/db/models/feature_flag.py",
  8568:       "title": "Register the feature flags router in the app in clinic-api/src/clinic_api/main.py",
  8569:       "description_md": "Register the feature flags router in the app in clinic-api/src/clinic_api/main.py",
  41207:       "description_md": "In the afternoon, a receptionist opens the \"Reminders failed\" screen and sees tomorrow's appointments, at their own clinic, whose reminder could not be delivered by any channel. They phone those patients. **Why this priority**: Release 2 (Should). It gives reception a safety net for the patients the system could not reach. **Independent Test**: Create tomorrow's appointments with failed, delivered, cancelled and not-reminded states at two clinics, sign in as a receptionist of one clinic and check the list. **Acceptance Scenarios**: 1. **Given** tomorrow has appointments marked \"reminder failed\", **When** a receptionist opens \"Reminders failed\", **Then** they see exactly those appointments at their own clinic with time, patient name, phone number, dentist, treatment and chosen channel. 2. **Given** a failed-reminder appointment is cancelled, **When** the list is refreshed, **Then** it no longer appears. 3. **Given** a receptionist of one clinic, **When** they open the list, **Then** they never see another clinic's appointments; the practice manager sees both clinics. 4. **Given** appointments whose reminders were delivered, are still queued, or were never created (booked less than 24 hours ahead), **When** the list is shown, **Then** they do not appear. 5. **Given** no reminder failed for tomorrow, **When** the list is opened, **Then** an empty state says so. 6. **Given** the Release 2 feature flag is off, **When** a user looks for the screen, **Then** it is not shown. ---",
  41246:           "text": "Given the Release 2 feature flag is off, When a user looks for the screen, Then it is not shown. (source: FR-033)"
  48350:       "description_md": "A signed-in patient opens \"Family\" on their account and adds a family member by giving a name and a birth year. They can add up to 5 family members. The new person shows in the list of people on the account, next to the patient themselves. The family member has no phone number and no sign-in of their own: they are a person on the account holder's account. **Why this priority**: Nothing else in this feature works until a family member exists. It is the core of FR-006. **Independent Test**: Sign in as a patient with no family members, add one with a name and birth year, and see them in the list. Add four more; the sixth attempt is refused with a clear message. Delivers a usable list of people on the account. **Acceptance Scenarios**: 1. **Given** a signed-in patient with fewer than 5 family members, **When** they enter a name and a valid birth year and confirm, **Then** the family member is saved on their account and appears in the list of people on the account. 2. **Given** a signed-in patient who already has 5 family members, **When** they try to add another, **Then** the system refuses, says that 5 family members is the limit, and the list is unchanged. 3. **Given** a signed-in patient on the add screen, **When** they leave the name empty or enter a birth year that is not a four-digit year in a plausible range, **Then** the system says what to correct and saves nothing. 4. **Given** a signed-in patient, **When** they add a family member, **Then** only a name and a birth year are stored for that person (no phone number, no other personal details). 5. **Given** the family-members feature flag is off, **When** a patient opens their account or sends a request to add a family member, **Then** the \"Family\" screen is not shown and the request is refused. ---",
  48384:           "text": "Given the family-members feature flag is off, When a patient opens their account or sends a request to add a family member, Then the \"Family\" screen is not shown and the request is refused. (source: FR-006)"
  52435:       "description_md": "A patient (or a family member the patient books for) who has had 2 no-shows in the last 6 months is told, when they try to book or reschedule online, that online booking is not available and is shown the clinic's phone number. Appointments they already have stay as they are. Each person is counted on their own: a family member's no-shows count against that family member, not against the account holder. **Why this priority**: This is the rule that discourages repeat no-shows, the clinic's biggest problem. Without it the other two stories have nothing to show or lift. **Independent Test**: Record 2 no-shows within 6 months for one test patient, then sign in as that patient and try to book and to reschedule; both are refused with the clinic phone number, while an existing booking is still listed and can be cancelled. Repeat for a family member on the same account and confirm the account holder is not blocked. **Acceptance Scenarios**: 1. **Given** a patient with 2 no-shows in the last 6 months, **When** they reach the step where they choose a dentist and slot, **Then** the system says online booking is not available and shows the phone number of the clinic they chose, and no booking is created. 2. **Given** a patient with 2 no-shows in the last 6 months and an upcoming booking, **When** they try to reschedule it online, **Then** the system says online rescheduling is not available and shows the phone number of that appointment's clinic, and the booking stays unchanged. 3. **Given** a patient with 2 no-shows in the last 6 months and upcoming bookings, **When** they view their appointments, **Then** all existing bookings are still listed and none is cancelled or changed by the block. 4. **Given** an account holder with a family member who has 2 no-shows in the last 6 months, **When** the account holder books online for themselves, **Then** the booking is accepted; **When** they try to book for that family member, **Then** it is refused as in scenario 1. 5. **Given** a patient with 1 no-show in the last 6 months, **When** they book or reschedule online, **Then** the booking proceeds as normal. 6. **Given** a patient whose older no-show falls out of the 6-month window so that fewer than 2 remain in the window, **When** they try to book online, **Then** the booking proceeds as normal without anyone lifting anything. 7. **Given** the Release 2 feature flag is off, **When** a patient with 2 no-shows in the last 6 months books or reschedules, **Then** the booking behaves as before this feature (not blocked). ---",
  52479:           "text": "Given the Release 2 feature flag is off, When a patient with 2 no-shows in the last 6 months books or reschedules, Then the booking behaves as before this feature (not blocked)"
  52649:       "description_md": "The practice manager opens a no-show report that shows, for each clinic and for each of the last 12 months, the number of no-shows and the no-show rate (no-shows divided by appointments that were not cancelled). The report is on screen only, with no export. **Why this priority**: It gives the manager the figure the clinic lacks today and the baseline for the TBD no-show target (ASM-015). It does not depend on the block, so it can ship and be tested on its own, but patients and reception feel the block first. **Independent Test**: Seed appointments across 2 clinics and several months with a known mix of statuses, open the report as the practice manager, and compare each clinic-month cell with hand-counted figures; confirm a receptionist and a patient cannot open it and that no export action exists. **Acceptance Scenarios**: 1. **Given** the practice manager is signed in, **When** they open the no-show report, **Then** they see one row per clinic and month for the last 12 months, each with the number of no-shows and the no-show rate. 2. **Given** a clinic-month with 40 appointments of which 4 were cancelled by the patient, 2 cancelled by the clinic and 3 are no-shows, **When** the report is shown, **Then** the rate is 3 divided by 34 (appointments not cancelled), shown as a percentage, and the no-show count is 3. 3. **Given** a walk-in booked as a normal appointment and marked arrived, **When** the report counts that month, **Then** the walk-in is counted among the appointments that were not cancelled. 4. **Given** a clinic-month with no appointments that were not cancelled, **When** the report is shown, **Then** the count is 0 and the rate is shown as \"no appointments\" rather than as a number or an error. 5. **Given** a patient whose personal data was deleted on request and whose appointment rows were anonymised, **When** the report is shown, **Then** the counts and rates are the same as before the deletion. 6. **Given** a receptionist or a patient or a dentist is signed in, **When** they try to open the report, **Then** access is refused. 7. **Given** the report is open, **When** the manager looks for a way to download or export it, **Then** none is offered. 8. **Given** the Release 2 feature flag is off, **When** the practice manager looks at the menu, **Then** the report screen is not shown. ---",
  52698:           "text": "Given the Release 2 feature flag is off, When the practice manager looks at the menu, Then the report screen is not shown"
