  9: **Input**: User description: "Family members on a patient account (Release 2). A patient can add up to 5 family members to their account (name and birth year) and book for any of them; each booking names the person it is for. Release 2 (Should), due 2027-03-19, about 2-3 weeks after the 1 March 2027 go-live; hidden by a feature flag until ready." (source: FR-006, US-006)
  27: 5. **Given** the family-members feature flag is off, **When** a patient opens their account or sends a request to add a family member, **Then** the "Family" screen is not shown and the request is refused. (source: FR-006)
  106: - **FR-011**: The family-member screens, the "who is it for" choice and the family-member operations MUST be available only while the Release 2 feature flag for family members is on; while it is off, booking is for the patient themselves only. (source: FR-006)
  131: - A-1: Release 2 (Should), due 2027-03-19, about 2-3 weeks after the 1 March 2027 go-live; screens and operations are hidden behind a feature flag until ready.
/outputs/clinic-test-2/specs/008-family-members/tasks.md:
  14: **Organization**: Tasks are grouped by user story. Source requirement: FR-006 (US-006); related FR-004, FR-015, FR-014, FR-027, FR-031, NFR-007. All code is behind the `family_members` feature flag (Release 2).
/outputs/clinic-test-2/specs/009-noshow-block-report/plan.md:
  9: Put the real repeat no-show rule behind the "is this person blocked?" check that online booking (feature 004) and rescheduling (feature 005) already call, let reception see and lift a block, and give the practice manager a 12-month no-show report per clinic. Backend: a new `cmp-noshow-policy` module (counts a person's no-shows in the last 6 months since their last lift, keeps `ent-no-show-block` rows, lifts) and a new `cmp-reporting` module (one grouped read through `cmp-booking`), plus small additions to `cmp-booking` (a no-show counting reader, the block check wired in on confirm) and `cmp-reception` (show and lift). Web: block notice on the booking and reschedule screens, a block banner and Lift action in the reception patient panel, and a no-show report screen for the practice manager. Everything sits behind one Release 2 feature flag. Counts are live queries over appointments and their history (no cache, no new table beyond `ent-no-show-block`), per the architecture.
/outputs/clinic-test-2/specs/009-noshow-block-report/research.md:
  50: - **Rationale**: FR-014, FR-016; architecture says R2 screens are hidden by a feature flag until their data is ready.
/outputs/clinic-test-2/specs/009-noshow-block-report/spec.md:
  9: **Input**: User description: "Repeat no-show block and no-show report (Release 2). Covers prd.md ids FR-025, FR-026, FR-032. A patient with 2 no-shows in the last 6 months cannot book or reschedule online; reception sees and lifts the block; the practice manager sees no-shows and the no-show rate per clinic and month for the last 12 months, on screen only. Release 2 (Should, due 2027-03-19, after the 1 March 2027 go-live), hidden by a feature flag until ready."
  13: No-shows are BrightSmile Dental's biggest problem. Today's no-show rate is not known (PRD "Questions to raise", item 1), so the no-show target is TBD and the first 2 months of app data are the baseline (ASM-015). This feature has two parts: a repeat no-show block on online booking (P-01 Patient, P-02 Receptionist) and a monthly no-show report (P-04 Practice manager). Both belong to Release 2 and stay hidden behind a feature flag until their data is ready. Two earlier features already call a "is this person blocked?" check on online booking and rescheduling and get "not blocked" until this feature exists; this feature puts the real rule behind that check without changing how existing bookings behave.
  33: 7. **Given** the Release 2 feature flag is off, **When** a patient with 2 no-shows in the last 6 months books or reschedules, **Then** the booking behaves as before this feature (not blocked).
  74: 8. **Given** the Release 2 feature flag is off, **When** the practice manager looks at the menu, **Then** the report screen is not shown.
  111: - **FR-016**: System MUST hide the block (its effect on booking and its reception actions) and the report screen behind a Release 2 feature flag until they are ready; with the flag off, booking and rescheduling behave as before this feature. (source: FR-025, FR-026, FR-032)
  131: - **SC-007**: With the feature flag off, 100% of existing booking and reschedule tests from earlier features still pass unchanged.
